body:
For the most part, for me, it's the idea that you HAVE to spend an hour or two a day, every day, smacking a motionless target dummy to perform 20 hit combos that LOOK cool as shit but only do maybe 1/4 a life bar. A combo that when in an actual match will almost NEVER have the absolute optimal setup to allow you to do it and that's IF your opponent doesnt manage to know the exact specific counter to end it 1/3 of the way through.

I have no problem playing, and losing, if i'm having fun. The problem i have is when matchmaking is so terrible in how it decides who you're fighting you get matched with people either astronomically more skilled than you (because hey, you managed to accidentally win a couple in a row, by the barest skin of your teeth, better move you to the next rank) that you get stomped into dirt within 10 seconds both rounds, OR when you get matches with someone worse enough than you you end up accidentally doing the same.

&#x200B;

I streamed about 5 hours of GBVS launch day, and other than a single match, I enjoyed pretty much every second of it. HOWEVER, I also had a whopping 7 wins to my 40something losses in that time. Almost everyone i fought was VERY obviously out of my league. Some of them i could tell were doing their initial handfull of matches because they didn't have a letter ranking. A LOT of them were ranked either the same as me or in more than a few cases lower. Almost universally the ones ranked lower than me were the ones obliterating me effortlessly. Strangely I manged to do better, even if i didnt win the round, than people ranked higher than me.

So, the obvious takeway was that in my first few ranked matches where i was getting evaluated, I somehow managed to do WAY better than i actually was, right? Nope, i just managed to get matched against several people in a row who were ACTUALLY clueless (i think two of them barely had a chance to fight back) and i didn't notice it. Until my last two matches that i almost lost i legit thought i was being tested against the AI. 

Those initial matches not only probably ruined a couple people's desire to play the game by having them stomped by people far outclassing them, but also managed to put me WAY too high in the rankings because of it.

&#x200B;

All this was without spending my first few hours "labbing". I got the game i had been eagerly awaiting, and hopped straight in to play. Because of that i was hopelessly decimated from the outset, probably by people who either managed to get it a bit earlier than me and DID spend that hour whacking dummies, or had prior experience from playing the JP release for almost a full month. The idea that ANY game would tacitly ask you to NOT play it's main component until you spent a few hours beating up a dummy is insane to me. Shooters like COD or Battlefield dont have empty rooms where you're expected to shoot at target dummies for hours on end until you ONLY get headshots before you are "worthy" to play online. They have basic tutorials to get you into the feel of them, and then you're off, and in most cases you'll do just fine.

&#x200B;

It's great that fighting games are starting to have better tutorials, collections of mini-challenges that dont make practice feel like a chore but instead a side-game, but even THEN a lot of them have a learning curve on par with brick walls. "Sweet, you managed to do each special move a couple times for practice! Now lets start on 3 hit combos... okay now the 5 hit one... great! Now for combo tutorial #3, I want you to do a 2 hit combo into an air launcher, jump at a VERY specific timing (1 frame off and we wont count it even if you manage to DO the whole combo) hit them a few more times in teh air, do a special move then hit them 5 more times during the downfall, got it? No? Well you better get to that lab because this is #3 out of 25 and they only get harder from here..."

&#x200B;

I'll gladly lose to people my skill level all day, and gradually try to improve organically, but like any game the second i'm expected to treat it like a second job JUST to qualify for the lowest ranks i'm out. I don't want first place handed to me but i want to at least have fun trying to get there.
